    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green. The change is complete.\n\n## What I did\n\nConsolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`, rejecting with 409 only on a whole-key match.\n\n**New files**\n- `function/owner/OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 shared helper `key(Owner)` deriving the key (null/blank email and householdId \u2192 empty segment; telephone already E.164-normalized by `BuildOwner`, email already lower-cased).\n- `function/owner/EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` \u2014 the single check: computes the new owner's key and compares it, whole, against every other owner's key.\n- `escalation/DuplicateIdentityException.java` + `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java` (409, `errors: [\"identityKey\"]`) + its escalation YAML.\n\n**Pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`)** \u2014 replaced `ensureUniqueTelephone \u2192 ensureUniqueEmail \u2192 ensureUniqueHousehold` with a single `ensureUniqueIdentity`, and moved `assignHousehold` *before* it so the new owner's `householdId` is part of the compared key.\n\n**Response (`Return 'identityKey'`)** \u2014 added a read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` and mapped it in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` via `OwnerIdentity.key(owner)`.\n\n**Removed** the now-consolidated `EnsureUnique{Telephone,Email,Household}` functions and the `Duplicate{Telephone,Email,Household}Exception` classes, handlers and escalation YAMLs; cleaned up the dangling javadoc references to them.\n\n**Behaviour change verified by the design:** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now produce different keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a 409. The acceptance test (`coreRejectsIdentityCollision`, two owners sharing a telephone \u2192 409) passes, and the full suite is green.\n\nOne note: the old handlers reported field-specific `errors` (e.g. `[\"telephone\"]`); the consolidated handler now reports `[\"identityKey\"]`, and the 409 responses remain undeclared in the OpenAPI spec (unchanged from before).",
